## PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
<https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0>

Copyright (c) 2026 KeenGuard Project Authors

## Purpose
This license allows you to use the software for noncommercial purposes for free, but requires a commercial license for any commercial use.

## Agreement
In order to receive this license, you have to agree to its rules. Those rules are both terms of that agreement and conditions to each of the licenses for copyright and patent by each licensor.

## Notices
You must ensure that everyone who gets a copy of any part of this software from you, with or without changes, also gets the text of this license or a link to <https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0>.

## Noncommercial License
Each licensor grants you a copyright license to use the software for noncommercial purposes.

## Noncommercial Purposes
A noncommercial purpose is a purpose that is not a commercial purpose.

A commercial purpose is any use that has as its purpose, or that is directed towards, commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

## Patent License
Each licensor grants you a patent license for the software for noncommercial purposes. The patent license covers each patent claim the licensor can license, or becomes able to license, that the software implements.

## Noncommercial Patent Purpose
The patent license covers only your use of the software for noncommercial purposes. For example, if you use the software for a commercial purpose, the patent license does not cover that use.

## Fair Use
You may have "fair use" rights for the software under the law. These licenses do not affect those rights.

## No Other Rights
These licenses do not cover any patent claims you infringe by changes to the software, or by combinations of the software with other software or hardware. These licenses do not cover any trademarks, names, or logos of any licensor.

## Clean Up
If you violate this agreement, your licenses from all licensors end immediately. However, if you're willing to clean up the violation, you can get the licenses back:

1. If you get a written notice from a licensor or anyone else who gets the software from a licensor about the violation, you can get the licenses back by cleaning up the violation within 30 days of receiving the notice.

2. If you don't get any written notice about the violation, you can get the licenses back by cleaning up the violation within 30 days of when you first recognized the violation.

## Automatic Re-grant
If you clean up a violation, your licenses will be reinstated retroactive to the date the licenses ended. However, if you violate this agreement again, or if you violate this agreement for more than 30 days after you first learn of the violation, your licenses end permanently.

## No Defense
Reinstatement of the licenses does not affect any claim of a licensor for breach of agreement or patent infringement for the period that the licenses were ended.

## Trade Secrets
Some software protected by this license may be provided in source code form, and some may be provided in compiled or binary form. These licenses give you no right to reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble any binary form of the software, except to the extent that you can't be prohibited by law.

## Disclaimer
As far as the law allows, the software comes as is, without any warranty or condition, and no licensor will be liable to anyone for any damages of any kind or for any reason, under any legal theory, arising out of this agreement or the use of the software.
